-- 2026-08-04 sweep repair #2 — 72 more aqar Buy prices proven understated vs the LIVE page.
-- Bounding sweep of the backfill.v1 capture class (231 at-risk + 150 random control, all fetched
-- live). Control arm: 0 truncations in 150 random rows → the class does NOT extend into the
-- general population. At-risk arm surfaced three defect shapes, all UNDERSTATING the price:
--   • 5 rows  ~1000x  — the thousands separator eaten (same class as migration 20260804184833)
--   • 20 rows ppm-as-total — «سعر المتر» stored as the total
--   • 47 rows 10-200x — the price scraped out of the ad's FREE-TEXT description (rental income,
--     mortgage amount, monthly rent) instead of the price slot; ratios arbitrary, so these were
--     NOT recoverable by arithmetic — each new value was read from that listing's live page.
-- Every value below came from an independent fetch of the listing's JSON-LD offers.price (76/76
-- pages returned a price). The 4 rows whose page differed by <2x were EXCLUDED as ordinary source
-- price changes and left to the crawler. Guarded by the current wrong value → idempotent.
-- price_per_meter is nulled on repaired rows: it had been re-derived from the broken total, so an
-- honest null beats a wrong rate; the next crawl repopulates it from the source.
